<h2 id="merge-branches">Merge branches</h2>

<p><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">$ git merge br-name</code> merges the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">br-name</code> branch into the current branch 
Adding <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">--no-ff</code> disables the fast-forward mode, meaning a new commit is created instead of just moving the HEAD pointer 
<code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">$ git merge --no-ff -m "merge with no-ff" dev</code> 
Before merging, you can use <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">git diff &lt;source_branch&gt; &lt;target_branch&gt;</code> to view the differences between the two branches</p>

